                  <provenance source="2905"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_224">Glastonbury, Somerset.
                        Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Borrowed from
                        Malmesbury by the abbot of Glastonbury in 1411, see the note on fol. 1v:
                        'Istum librum recepit mutuo dominus abbas Glaston. xiiij die mensis
                        februarii anno domini millesimo. ccccmo. xj restituendum ad festum Sancti
                        Michaelis proxime futurum'.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Trinity by John Whitgift, archbishop
                     of Canterbury (1530/31?--1604).</provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="3902"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_360">Malmesbury, Wiltshire.
                        Benedictine Abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St Aldhelm</orgName><p>On
                        flyleaf: 'Istum librum recepit mutuo dominus J. Exon. episcopus [=
                        Grandison] ab Abbate Malmisberi Anno Domini mo. ccc. xxxij prima die Julij.
                        Et restituit eundem priori de Pyltone anno sequenti, prima die Maij'
                        (borrowed in 1411 by the Abbot of Glastonbury).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance cert="low" source="4432"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_447">Pilton, Devon. Benedictine
                        priory of St Mary the Virgin; cell of Malmesbury</orgName><p>Borrowed from
                        Malmesbury by bp. John Grandison, and returned by him to the Prior of Pilton
                        in 1333.</p></provenance>
